\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Problem Statement\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs32 \cf2 Business Entity Resolution Challenge\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 \cb3 In large-scale commercial platforms, business identity data arrives from multiple independent sources \'97 each contributing partial, noisy fragments of information about the same real-world entities. These fragments share no common identifiers, and the challenge of determining which records refer to the same business is known as Entity Resolution (ER). Your challenge is to build an ML solution that, given business records from 3 independent data sources with noisy and inconsistent fields, determines which records across sources refer to the same real-world business entity.\cb1 \
\cb3 Source 1 is the deduplicated reference source. Your task is to find all matching records from Source 2 and Source 3 for each Source 1 entity. A Source 1 entity may match zero, one, or many records from Source 2 and Source 3.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf2 \cb3 File Format\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 All files in this challenge are tab-separated (
\f2 .tsv
\f0 ), and your submissions must be tab-separated too.
\f1\b0\fs28  Tabs are used because business addresses and the ID list columns both contain commas. Read them with an explicit tab separator, for example:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs30 \cf4 \cb3 \strokec4 import pandas as pd\
df = pd.read_csv("dataset/train/train_source1.tsv", sep="\\t")\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Reading a 
\f3 .tsv
\f1  without 
\f3 sep="\\t"
\f1  will silently produce a single column containing the whole line.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs35 \cf2 \cb3 Data Description:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 \cb3 Each source file (
\f3 *_source1.tsv
\f1 , 
\f3 *_source2.tsv
\f1 , 
\f3 *_source3.tsv
\f1 ) has the following columns:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 entity_id:
\f1\b0\fs28  Unique identifier for the record. The prefix indicates the source \'97 
\f3 S1-
\f1 , 
\f3 S2-
\f1 , or 
\f3 S3-
\f1 .\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs30 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 business_name:
\f1\b0\fs28  Name of the business entity (may contain abbreviations, legal suffixes, typos, transliterations)\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs30 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 business_address:
\f1\b0\fs28  Address of the business (may contain partial addresses, format variations, missing components, landmark-based references)\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs30 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 country:
\f1\b0\fs28  Country label for the record. The 
\f0\b\fs30 training
\f1\b0\fs28  data covers 
\f3 US
\f1  and 
\f3 India
\f1 . The 
\f0\b\fs30 test
\f1\b0\fs28  set additionally contains a third country, 
\f3 France
\f1 , that does 
\f0\b\fs30 not
\f1\b0\fs28  appear in the training data. Treat 
\f3 country
\f1  as an open set of string labels: do 
\f0\b\fs30 not
\f1\b0\fs28  hard-code, filter, or one-hot your pipeline to only 
\f3 \{US, India\}
\f1 , and remember that every test entity \'97 
\f3 France
\f1  included \'97 must appear in your submission.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb3 There is no separate 
\f4\i source
\f1\i0  column \'97 a record's source is given by its 
\f3 entity_id
\f1  prefix (
\f3 S1-
\f1 /
\f3 S2-
\f1 /
\f3 S3-
\f1 ) and by which file it appears in.\cb1 \
\cb3 The ground truth file (
\f3 train_ground_truth.tsv
\f1 ) has two columns:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs30 \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 source1_entity_id:
\f1\b0\fs28  The 
\f3 entity_id
\f1  of a Source 1 record\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs30 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 matched_entity_ids:
\f1\b0\fs28  Comma-separated list of matching 
\f3 entity_id
\f1 s from Source 2 and/or Source 3 (empty when the entity has no matches)\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa300\partightenfactor0

